{"id":"word:hebrew:H5650","type":"word","title":"עֶבֶד","subtitle":"H5650 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a servant","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עֶבֶד (H5650) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 803 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עֶבֶד (ʻebed) means a servant First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 34."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עֶבֶד","transliteration":"ʻebed","pronunciation":"eh'-bed","strong":"H5650","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5650","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["עַבְדֵ֣י","עַבְדְּ/ךָ֔","עַבְדֶּ֑/ךָ","עֲבָדָ֖י/ו","עֲבָדָ֔י/ו"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",141],["HNcmpc/Sp3ms",98],["HNcmpc/Sp2ms",69],["HNcmpc",68],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",52],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",43],["HNcmsc",38],["HNcmpa",38],["HNcmsa",32],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp2ms",28]]},"definitions":{"short":"a servant","usage":"× bondage, bondman, (bond-) servant, (man-) servant.","full":"H5650. ebed I. עֶ֫בֶד 799 noun masculine slave, servant (on formation Lag BN 77 ); — ׳ע Gen 9:25 +, עָ֑בֶד 44:10 +; suffix עַבְדִּי 26:24 +; עַבְדְּךָ 19:19 +; עַבְדֶּ֫ךָ 18:3 +; plural עֲבָדִים 9:25 +, עַבְדֵי 21:25 +, suffix עֲבָדַי Lev 25:42 +, עַבְדֵיכֶם Josh 9:11 +, etc.; — 1 slave, servant of household Gen 39:17 , 19 ; 41:12 ; 50:2 ; Exod 21:2 +; man-servant , || אמה 20:10 ; Lev 25:6 ; Deut 5:14 ; Job 31:13 +; || שׁפחה Gen 12:16 ; 32:6 ; Jer 34:11 ; Isa 14:2 +; + אדון Deut 23:16 ; Isa 24:2 ; Mal 1:6 +; כֶּסֶף מִקְנַת Exod 12:44 or בַּיִת יְלִיד Jer 2:14 ; עֲבָדִים עֶבֶד servant of servants, humblest servant , Gen 9:25 ; עֲבָדִים בֵּית house of slaves , especially Israel in Egypt Exod 13:3 , 14 (D ?) Deut 5:6 ; 6:12 ; 7:8 ; 8:14 ; 13:6 ; 13:11 ; Josh 24:17 ; Judg 6:8 ; Jer 34:13 ; Micah 6:4 ; ב(ארץׅ מצרים היית עבד כי וזכרת and thou shalt remember that thou wast a slave in (the land of) Egypt Deut 5:15 ; 15:15 ; 16:12 ; 24:18 , 22 ; king of Babylon is slave to ׳י Jer 25:9 ; 27:6 ; 43:10 ; the borrower to the lender Prov 22:7 ; figurative of beast Job 40:28; of things Gen 47:19 . 2 Subjects , of chief Gen 26:15 , 19 , 25 , 32 ; 27:37 ; 32:17 (twice in verse) +; of king 21:25 ; Exodus 7:28; Exodus 7:29; 1Kin 9:27 ; Deut 29:1 +; vassal kings 2Sam 10:19 ; tributary nations 8:2 , 6 , 14 = 1Chr 18:2 , 6 , 13 ; specifically officers of king 1Sam 19:1 ; 21:8 ; 2Sam 11:13 ; Prov 14:35 +; פַרְעֹה עַבְדֵי Gen 40:20 ; 41:10 ; ׳ע שָׁאוּל 1Sam 16:17 ; 18:22 ; 28:7 ; ׳ע הַמֶּלֶךְ 1Kin 1:47 ; Est 3:3 +; הַמֶּלֶךְ עֶבֶד 2Kin 22:12 2Chr 34:20 (a court offical); opposed to שַׂר Prov 19:10 ; Eccl 10:7 ; מֶלֶךְ Prov 30:22 ; ambassadors Num 22:18 ; 2Sam 10:2 ; soldiers of army 1Sam 17:8 ; 25:10 ; 2Sam 2:12 , + officers of army 1Sam 29:3 ; 1Kin 11:26 ; 2Kin 25:8 ; Isa 36:9 . 3 Servants, worshippers , of God: יהוה עַבְדֵי 2Kin 9:7 ; 10:23 ; Isa 54:17 , compare Gen 50:17 ; Isa 56:6 ; עֲבָדָיו Deut 32:36 = Psa 135:14 ; Isa 65:15 ; 66:14 ; Psalm 34:23; Psalm 69:37; Neh 2:20 ; || עַמּוֺ Psa 105:25 compare Deut 32:43 ; עֲבָּדַי Isa 65:8-9 , 13 (twice in verse); Isa 69:13; Isa 69:14; עֲבָדֶיךָ 1Kin 8:23 ; Isa 63:17 (|| נחלתך שִׁבְטֵי ), Psa 89:51 ; 90:13 ; 90:16 ; 102:15 ; Psalm 102:29; 119:91 ; 79:2 ; 79:10 (|| חֲסִידֶיךָ ); delivered from Egypt Lev 25:42 , 55 (twice in verse); 26:13 (P); עַבְדְּךָ Psa 119:125 ; 143:2 , || בֶּןאֲֿמָתֶ֑ךָ 86:16 ; 116:16 (twice in verse); specifically angels Job 4:18 ; and ancient worthies, patriarchs Exod 32:13 (J) Deut 9:27 ; Abraham Gen 26:24 (J) Psa 105:6 ; 105:42 ; Isaac Gen 24:14 (J); Jacob, Israel Ezek 28:25 ; 37:25 ; 1Chr 16:13 ; Moses Exod 14:31 ; Josh 18:7 (J) Num 12:7-8 , (E) Deut 34:5 (?) Josh 1:1-2 , 7 , 13 , 15 ; 8:31 , 33 ; 9:24 ; 11:12 , 15 ; 12:6 (twice in verse); 13:8 ; 14:7 ; 22:2 , 4 , 5 (all D), 1Kin 8:53 , 56 ; 2Kin 18:12 ; 21:8 ; 1Chr 6:34 ; 2Chr 1:3 ; 24:6 , 9 ; Neh 1:8 ; 9:14 ; 10:30 ; Psa 105:26 ; Malachi 3:22; Dan 9:11 ; Joshua Josh 24:29 (E) Judg 2:8 ; Caleb Num 14:24 (J); Job Job 1:8 ; 2:3 ; 42:7-8 , (3 t. in verse); David 2Sam 3:18 ; 7:5 , 8 , 26 27 t.; Hezekiah 2Chr 32:16 ; Zerubbabel Hag 2:23 ; Eliakim Isa 22:20 . &#8212; The צֶמַח Zech 3:8 ; compare 6:12 is also servant of ׳י as Messianic builder of temple (see Br MP 442 ff ). 4 Servant of ׳י , in a special sense: of Levitical singers using benedictions in temple Psa 113:1 ; 134:1 ; 135:1 ; usually of prophets, הַנְּבִיאִים עֲבָדַי my servants the prophets 2Kin 9:7 ; 17:13 ; Jer 7:25 ; 26:5 ; 29:19 ; 35:15 ; 44:4 ; Ezek 38:17 ; Zech 1:6 ; הַנְּבִיאִים עֲבָדָיו 2Kin 17:23 ; 21:10 ; 24:2 ; Jer 25:4 ; Amos 3:7 ; Dan 9:10 ; הנביאים עֲבָדֶיךָ Ezra 9:11 ; Dan 9:6 ; specifically Ahia 1Kin 14:18 ; 15:29 ; Elijah 2Kin 9:36 ; 10:10 ; Jonah 14:25 ; Isaiah Isa 20:3 ; עַבְדּוֺ , || מלאכיו 44:26 ; as one calling to fear ׳י 50:10 . 5 Israel as a people is servant of יִשְׂרָאֵל ׳׃י Isa 41:8-9 , 44:21 (twice in verse); 49:3 ; Psa 136:22 ; יעקב Isa 44:1 ; 44:2 ; 45:4 ; 48:20 ; Jer 30:10 ; 46:27 ; Jeremiah 47:28; עַבְדִּי = יהוה עֶבֶד , || מַלְאָכִי , as having a mission to the nations Isa 42:19 (twice in verse); and chosen as witness of ׳י 43:10 . But there is also an ideal servant chosen and endowed with the divine Spirit to be a covenant of Israel and a light of the nations 42:1 (compare 42:2-6 ); formed to bring back Jacob, raise up the tribes, and become salvation to the end of the earth 49:5-6 , 7 ; bearing the sins of all as a lamb and a trespass-offering, and yet prospering and justifying many as interposing martyr 52:13 ; 53:11 : many understand of ideal Israel, contrasted with the actual; al. of personified || with Zion the wife and mother, distinguished from unworthy Israel as Zion from her apostate children; al. of ideal prophetic writer; al. of ideal prophetic person; al. (especially in Isaiah 53) of an actual prophecy known to writer and his readers; [in any case it is Messianic, see Matt 8:16-17 , 12:16-21 ; Luke 4:17-22 ; Phil 2:5-11 ]; see De Isa ii. 174 Da Expos. 1884, 358 ff. Di Du Che and others on Isaiah 42; Isaiah 53, Dr Is 168 ff. Br MP 345 ff. , also Gie Beitr. 146 ff. Berthol Isaiah 53 . 6 In polite address of equals or superiors the Hebrews used עַבְדְּךָ thy servant = 1 person singular, I , Gen 18:3 ; 1Sam 20:7-8 , (twice in verse); 2Kin 8:13 +; עֲבָדֶיךָ thy servants = we Gen 42:11 ; Isa 36:11 ; also עַבְדּוֺ his servant = I , 1Sam 26:18-19 , 2Sam 14:22 ; 24:21 +; also in addressing God, especially in prayer Exod 4:10 ; Num 11:11 ; Judg 15:18 ; 1Sam 3:9-10 , 25:39 ; 2Sam 24:10 ; Psa 19:12 ; 19:14 ; 27:9 ; 31:17 ; 35:27 ; 69:18 ; 109:28 ; 143:2 +. 7 Phrases are: עבד ( היה ), with לְ person, become servant to Gen 9:26-27 , 44:10 , 16 , 17 , 33 ; 47:19 , 26 (J) Deut 6:21 ; 15:17 ; 2Sam 8:14 ; 2Kin 17:3 ; 24:1 ; 1Chr 18:2 , 6 , 13 ; 2Chr 10:7 ; Prov 11:29 ; 12:9 ; 22:7 ; לעבד היה , with לְ person, Gen 44:9 (J) 50:18 (E) 1Sam 8:17 ; 17:9 (twice in verse); 27:12 ; 2Sam 8:2 , 6 ; Jer 34:16 ; לעבדים כבשׁ 2Chr 28:10 ; Neh 5:5 ; Jer 34:11 ; לע ׳לקח Gen 43:18 (J) 2Kin 4:1 ; Job 40:28.","rootNote":"from 5647 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 34","keyReferences":["1Chr 2 34","1Chr 2 35","1Chr 6 34","1Chr 16 13","1Chr 17 4","1Chr 17 7","1Chr 17 17","1Chr 17 18"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":803,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 2 34","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עֶ֥בֶד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 35","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":35,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַבְדּ֖/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 34","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עֶ֥בֶד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 13","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַבְדּ֔/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 17 4","book":"1Chr","chapter":17,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַבְדִּ֔/